@id: scene.028_ragnarok
@when: Unknown.scene_028_ragnarok
@where: Realm/Physical/Unknown
@scope: narrative
@entities: [Geralt, Oreck]
@region: Unknown
@environment: cosmic
@terrain_family: cosmic
@spatial_scale_hint: massive

=segments:
  - line: 1
    type: narration
    text: "book 5"
  - line: 2
    type: narration
    text: "chapter 028-ragnarok"
  - line: 4
    type: narration
    text: "The Warning"
  - line: 6
    type: narration
    text: "Four weeks."
  - line: 8
    type: narration
    text: "Twenty-eight days since Anunnaki patrol had witnessed the compound's impossible defiance, since they'd fled Earth to report what should never have been possible—slaves speaking, Overseer dead, resistance organized and successful."
  - line: 10
    type: narration
    text: "Twenty-eight days of preparation."
  - line: 11
    type: narration
    text: "Of training."
  - line: 12
    type: narration
    text: "Of transforming freed slaves into something approaching fighting force."
  - line: 13
    type: narration
    text: "Of Geralt learning to coordinate with adolescent armor that remained unpredictable despite Zaron's best efforts and the Applicator's technical mediation."
  - line: 15
    type: narration
    text: "Twenty-eight days of waiting for consequences they all knew were coming."
  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood watch on the compound's eastern boundary—the direction from which threats had historically arrived, the approach any sensible military force would use given terrain advantages and sight lines."
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "The twin suns were descending, painting the desert in shades that made distance difficult to judge, shadows stretching long enough to hide entire armies if positioned correctly."
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "Beside him, Oreck scanned the horizon with predator's awareness that centuries of military service had ingrained too deeply to ever fully fade."
  - line: 22
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"It's been four weeks,\""
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "the reptilian said quietly, breaking silence that had stretched for nearly an hour. \"Standard Anunnaki protocol for anomaly assessment and response is thirty days. Sometimes less if the threat is deemed severe enough.\""
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt the armor shift slightly around him—Zaron's consciousness stirring at mention of potential combat, the Applicator running probability calculations that produced numbers neither comforting nor surprising."
  - line: 27
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You think they're coming back.\""
  - line: 29
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know they're coming back.\""
  - line: 30
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's vertical pupils contracted, focusing on something at horizon's edge that Geralt's merely human vision couldn't yet distinguish. \"The question isn't if, but what they're bringing. We killed an Overseer. Broke a compound. Proved resistance is possible. They'll send enough force to ensure it never happens again.\""
  - line: 32
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"How much force?\""
  - line: 34
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Depends on who's responding.\""
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's claws flexed unconsciously—combat reflexes activating despite conscious control. \"If it's Anunnaki military responding to Overseer's death, we'll face standard garrison. Thirty to forty soldiers, maybe two commanders, heavy weapons but conventional tactics.\""
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "He paused, and something in his posture shifted—awareness sharpening beyond normal alertness into recognition of specific threat."
  - line: 39
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"But that's not Anunnaki ship configuration.\""
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt followed Oreck's gaze, and now he could see it—distant gleam that suggested metal catching fading sunlight, shape that grew more distinct with each passing moment."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "Not golden angular Anunnaki design, but something sleeker, more elegant, carrying authority that transcended simple military function."
  - line: 44
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Oreck
    text: "\"Federation,\""
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "Host, the Applicator's presence consolidated with sharp attention."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "Galactic Federation operates under different protocols than Anunnaki military."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "They're authorized to confiscate unauthorized artifacts, to arrest individuals violating cosmic law, to enforce regulations that supersede local authority."
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "They can take the armor."
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "Legally."
  - line: 52
    type: narration
    text: "And we would have no recourse."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt Zaron's consciousness bristle at the implication—fragmented god-consciousness that had sacrificed everything to become weapon wouldn't accept being \"confiscated\" like contraband."
  - line: 56
    type: narration
    text: "Over my scattered fragments, Zaron snarled."
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "No bureaucrat takes what I've become."
  - line: 59
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"Should we hide?\""
  - line: 61
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Too late.\""
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck gestured toward the approaching ship. \"They're already scanning. Already cataloging. They know we're here, know we're armed, know we're organized beyond what freed slave population should be.\""
  - line: 64
    type: narration
    text: "The reptilian turned to face Geralt directly, vertical pupils showing concern that transcended tactical assessment."
  - line: 66
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Close your helm. Now. Before they get visual confirmation. If they identify you—if they record your face and correlate it with the armor—you'll be hunted across the galaxy for the rest of your existence.\""
  - line: 68
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's hand rose toward the helm controls, muscle memory prepared to trigger the sealing mechanism that would hide his features behind draconic faceplate."
  - line: 70
    type: narration
    text: "Then stopped."
  - line: 72
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"No.\""
  - line: 74
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Geralt—\""
  - line: 76
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I said no.\""
  - line: 77
    type: narration
    text: "He lowered his hand, meeting Oreck's gaze with certainty that came from consciousness contested by two other entities, from self-awareness forged through trials that tested character rather than simple strength. \"I'm not hiding. Not my face. Not what I've done. Not who I've become.\""
  - line: 79
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"They'll flag you. Your identity will be recorded, distributed, marked as enemy of galactic order. Every bounty hunter, every Federation enforcer, every Anunnaki who wants revenge—they'll all know exactly who you are.\""
  - line: 81
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Good.\""
  - line: 82
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's voice carried conviction that surprised even himself. \"Let them know. I freed these people. I killed the Overseer. I claimed this armor. I'm not ashamed of any of it, and I won't hide behind a mask like I did something wrong.\""
  - line: 84
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck stared at him for long moment, then made sound that might have been laugh or sigh or resignation to inevitable consequences of partnering with someone whose defiance transcended survival instinct."
  - line: 86
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Then we face them together. Openly. And deal with whatever follows.\""
  - line: 88
    type: narration
    text: "The Federation ship descended—approach vector calculated for maximum intimidation, engines generating pressure waves that kicked up sand and announced authority before single word was spoken."
  - line: 89
    type: narration
    text: "It settled fifty yards from the compound's boundary, landing struts extending with mechanical precision that spoke to technology centuries beyond anything Earth possessed."
  - line: 91
    type: narration
    text: "A ramp descended, and from the ship's interior—they emerged."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "Six figures."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "Not soldiers, though they carried themselves with military discipline."
  - line: 95
    type: narration
    text: "Not diplomats, though their bearing suggested authority beyond simple force."
  - line: 96
    type: narration
    text: "Enforcers."
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "Auditors."
  - line: 98
    type: narration
    text: "Beings who existed to ensure galactic law was maintained regardless of local circumstances or moral considerations."
  - line: 100
    type: narration
    text: "The lead figure was tall—impossibly tall, easily eight feet in height—humanoid but clearly not human."
  - line: 101
    type: narration
    text: "Skin that gleamed like polished obsidian, eyes that were solid white without pupil or iris, features that suggested both beauty and complete absence of empathy."
  - line: 102
    type: narration
    text: "Robes that seemed woven from starlight itself, carrying rank insignia Geralt didn't recognize but understood instinctively meant authority that superseded planetary governments."
  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "Behind the leader, five others—different species, different builds, all carrying scanning equipment and data tablets that glowed with information being collected in real-time."
  - line: 106
    type: narration
    text: "The leader's white eyes fixed on Geralt—on the armor, on his exposed face, on the wing-mounts and scales and technology that screamed Aeon Keeper origin."
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "When it spoke, the voice carried harmonics that suggested multiple speakers despite single source:"
  - line: 110
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I am Enforcer Vel'thara of the Galactic Federation Compliance Division. We are here to verify Anunnaki evacuation protocols have been properly executed and to assess any irregularities requiring corrective action.\""
  - line: 112
    type: narration
    text: "The white eyes never blinked, never wavered from Geralt's face."
  - line: 114
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You are in possession of unauthorized Aeon Keeper artifact. Surrender the Dragon Mail immediately for confiscation and await transport to Federation processing facility for questioning regarding acquisition method and intended usage.\""
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt the armor tense around him—Zaron's consciousness reacting to threat of separation, the Applicator calculating probability of successful resistance, his own will hardening into refusal that transcended rational thought."
  - line: 118
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"No.\""
  - line: 120
    type: narration
    text: "The single word hung in air between them—defiance given sound, rebellion distilled into syllable that carried weight beyond its brevity."
  - line: 122
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara's expression didn't change—couldn't change, given features that seemed carved from living stone rather than formed through biological processes."
  - line: 124
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"That was not request. That was statement of legal requirement under Galactic Federation Artifact Control Regulation, Section 7, Subsection 12. Unauthorized possession of Aeon Keeper technology constitutes Class-1 violation punishable by artifact confiscation and mandatory detention.\""
  - line: 126
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"I don't care about your regulations,\""
  - line: 128
    type: narration
    text: "One of the other Federation personnel—shorter, with crystalline features that suggested silicon-based biology—stepped forward, data tablet glowing with information being compiled in real-time."
  - line: 130
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Subject identification in progress,\""
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "it announced in voice like wind chimes. \"Species: Human. Origin: Earth, Sol System. Former designation: Slave 7-Alpha-9327. Current self-designation: Geralt. Genetic modifications detected—unauthorized vocal capability restoration, neural pathway alterations suggesting Nephoretti intervention.\""
  - line: 133
    type: narration
    text: "The crystalline being's features shifted into what might have been surprise."
  - line: 135
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Additional anomaly detected: Anunnaki Applicator construct present in subject's neural tissue. Symbiotic rather than controlling. Unprecedented behavioral deviation from standard operational parameters.\""
  - line: 137
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara's attention shifted fractionally—white eyes showing first hint of something beyond cold assessment."
  - line: 139
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You carry Anunnaki control device willingly? Explain.\""
  - line: 141
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"It's complicated,\""
  - line: 143
    type: narration
    text: "Very complicated, it muttered."
  - line: 145
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Irrelevant,\""
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara continued. \"The artifact must be surrendered. The Applicator must be extracted. You will be processed through standard Federation protocols for individuals found in violation of multiple galactic statutes.\""
  - line: 148
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And the others?\""
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt gestured toward the compound, toward three hundred freed slaves who'd gathered to watch confrontation, toward Mika and the Five and all the others who'd claimed voices and names and lives that transcended designation. \"What happens to them?\""
  - line: 151
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"They will be relocated to appropriate facilities pending determination of their status. The Anunnaki evacuation order remains in effect. This compound will be sealed and decommissioned. All parties will comply with Federation directives.\""
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "Something cold settled into Geralt's chest—recognition that this being, this enforcer of cosmic law, viewed conscious beings as problems requiring processing rather than people deserving consideration."
  - line: 155
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"No,\""
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara's expression remained unchanged, but something in its posture shifted—recognition that compliance would not be achieved through declarations of authority."
  - line: 159
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Then you leave us no choice. Enforcement protocols activate. Subject designated hostile. Artifact confiscation to proceed through application of necessary force.\""
  - line: 161
    type: narration
    text: "The other five Federation personnel moved with synchronized precision—weapons emerging from concealed holsters, energy fields activating around their forms, positioning that suggested military training despite civilian designation."
  - line: 163
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt the armor respond—Zaron's consciousness flooding with readiness that bordered on eagerness, the Applicator's calculations shifting from probability assessment to tactical analysis, his own body tensing with anticipation of violence he'd hoped to avoid but accepted as inevitable."
  - line: 165
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Last chance,\""
  - line: 166
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara said without emotion. \"Surrender peacefully. Minimize casualties. Accept processing.\""
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's answer was simple:"
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "He raised his armored hand—scales gleaming in doubled sunlight, power radiating from technology that had been prepared for exactly this moment—and channeled telekinetic force that would have been crude weeks before but had grown more refined through practice and partnership with consciousnesses that understood power beyond normal human capacity."
  - line: 172
    type: narration
    text: "The sand between them erupted—wall of silicon and minerals rising to block sight lines, to create barrier that bought seconds of tactical advantage."
  - line: 174
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"ORECK!\""
  - line: 176
    type: narration
    text: "The reptilian didn't argue, didn't question—simply moved with speed that belied his massive form, herding freed slaves toward structures that might provide protection from energy weapons and Federation enforcement protocols."
  - line: 178
    type: narration
    text: "Through the settling sand, Vel'thara's voice carried with unchanged calmness:"
  - line: 180
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Subject identified as hostile. Designation assigned: RAGNAROK. Threat level: Maximum. Enforcement personnel—neutralize with extreme prejudice. Artifact confiscation is secondary to threat elimination.\""
  - line: 182
    type: narration
    text: "Ragnarok?"
  - line: 183
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron asked with confusion."
  - line: 184
    type: narration
    text: "What kind of designation is—"
  - line: 186
    type: narration
    text: "Norse mythology, the Applicator supplied."
  - line: 187
    type: narration
    text: "End of world."
  - line: 188
    type: narration
    text: "Twilight of gods."
  - line: 189
    type: narration
    text: "Apocalyptic destruction."
  - line: 190
    type: narration
    text: "They're calling us the end of their order."
  - line: 192
    type: narration
    text: "I like it, Zaron decided."
  - line: 194
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Can we focus?\""
  - line: 195
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt snapped, then threw himself sideways as energy bolt tore through space he'd occupied heartbeat before."
  - line: 197
    type: narration
    text: "The battle began in earnest."
  - line: 199
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 201
    type: narration
    text: "The Trial"
  - line: 203
    type: narration
    text: "The Federation enforcers moved with precision that spoke to training measured in decades, to coordination that transcended verbal communication, to capability that made them far more dangerous than simple military force."
  - line: 205
    type: narration
    text: "Energy weapons blazed—not crude projectiles but focused particle beams that could punch through armor, disrupt shields, or simply vaporize targets depending on setting selected."
  - line: 206
    type: narration
    text: "The crystalline being's attacks carried additional property—each strike that missed Geralt impacted sand and created glass sculptures, deadly art that could impale or entangle."
  - line: 208
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt dodged—armor responding with increasing confidence as Zaron learned combat rhythms, as the Applicator provided tactical analysis, as three consciousnesses began functioning as unified system rather than competing entities."
  - line: 210
    type: narration
    text: "But the armor was still adolescent."
  - line: 211
    type: narration
    text: "Still learning."
  - line: 212
    type: narration
    text: "Still prone to fear responses that could override tactical necessity."
  - line: 214
    type: narration
    text: "A Federation enforcer—this one vaguely reptilian but smaller than Oreck, faster, covered in scales that shifted colors to match surroundings—appeared from Geralt's blind spot, energy blade materializing in clawed hand."
  - line: 216
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt spun to block—armor responding to intention—"
  - line: 218
    type: narration
    text: "—and froze."
  - line: 220
    type: narration
    text: "Completely."
  - line: 221
    type: narration
    text: "Utterly."
  - line: 222
    type: narration
    text: "Every system locking simultaneously as Zaron's consciousness detected threat level that triggered self-preservation protocols deeper than conscious control."
  - line: 224
    type: narration
    text: "DANGER, Zaron broadcast with panic that infected shared awareness."
  - line: 225
    type: narration
    text: "Too close, too fast, can't process, need to—"
  - line: 227
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"ZARON, NO!\""
  - line: 228
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt screamed, but his body didn't respond—armor had seized control, was initiating emergency protocols that involved fleeing rather than fighting."
  - line: 230
    type: narration
    text: "The energy blade descended—would have taken his head clean off if Oreck hadn't materialized from nowhere, massive clawed hand grabbing the Federation enforcer and hurling it away with force that sent the being tumbling across sand."
  - line: 232
    type: narration
    text: "Sorry!"
  - line: 233
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron yelped."
  - line: 234
    type: narration
    text: "I'm trying!"
  - line: 235
    type: narration
    text: "The fear response is automatic!"
  - line: 236
    type: narration
    text: "I can't—"
  - line: 238
    type: narration
    text: "Override initiated, the Applicator announced, presence flooding through armor's systems with authority that came from understanding machines at fundamental level."
  - line: 239
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron, I'm suppressing your panic response."
  - line: 240
    type: narration
    text: "Trust me."
  - line: 241
    type: narration
    text: "Let me handle threat assessment while you focus on animation."
  - line: 243
    type: narration
    text: "But—"
  - line: 245
    type: narration
    text: "TRUST ME."
  - line: 247
    type: narration
    text: "The armor unlocked, movement returning with jarring suddenness."
  - line: 248
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stumbled, barely catching himself before another energy bolt could capitalize on vulnerability."
  - line: 250
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"We need better communication!\""
  - line: 252
    type: narration
    text: "Understood, from both simultaneously."
  - line: 254
    type: narration
    text: "The coordination improved marginally—enough that Geralt could engage rather than simply survive, could counterattack rather than only dodge."
  - line: 256
    type: narration
    text: "He channeled telekinesis through the armor—the Applicator's presence amplifying power, Zaron's consciousness providing animation that made gestures more dramatic than necessary but undeniably effective."
  - line: 257
    type: narration
    text: "Sand rose in waves, creating barriers and projectiles, obscuring sight lines and forcing Federation enforcers to divide attention between multiple threats."
  - line: 259
    type: narration
    text: "But there were six of them and only one of him, and they were coordinated while his armor remained unpredictable despite improvements."
  - line: 261
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara stood at distance, observing, white eyes tracking every movement with assessment that went beyond simple tactical evaluation."
  - line: 262
    type: narration
    text: "Studying."
  - line: 263
    type: narration
    text: "Learning."
  - line: 264
    type: narration
    text: "Preparing countermeasures that would make second encounter far more difficult than first."
  - line: 266
    type: narration
    text: "One of the Federation enforcers—humanoid but with skin that seemed composed of living shadow, features barely distinguishable from darkness itself—moved with speed that suggested teleportation rather than normal locomotion."
  - line: 267
    type: narration
    text: "It appeared beside Geralt, weapon rising—"
  - line: 269
    type: narration
    text: "The armor's wing-mounts suddenly deployed."
  - line: 271
    type: narration
    text: "Not deliberately."
  - line: 272
    type: narration
    text: "Not through conscious command."
  - line: 273
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron's consciousness had decided autonomously that flight was superior defensive option, that escaping upward would remove them from immediate threat."
  - line: 275
    type: narration
    text: "The wings caught air with force that lifted Geralt off his feet, that sent him tumbling skyward in completely uncontrolled ascent that was equal parts terrifying and humiliating."
  - line: 277
    type: narration
    text: "WHAT ARE YOU DOING?"
  - line: 278
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt screamed mentally."
  - line: 280
    type: narration
    text: "ESCAPING!"
  - line: 281
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron replied with logic that was technically sound but tactically disastrous."
  - line: 282
    type: narration
    text: "They can't hit us if we're airborne!"
  - line: 284
    type: narration
    text: "I DON'T KNOW HOW TO FLY YET!"
  - line: 286
    type: narration
    text: "Oh."
  - line: 287
    type: narration
    text: "Right."
  - line: 288
    type: narration
    text: "That's... that's a problem."
  - line: 290
    type: narration
    text: "The ascent became tumble—wings folding and unfolding randomly as Zaron tried to figure out aerodynamics on the fly, literally, with predictable results."
  - line: 291
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt spun through air like leaf caught in storm, completely disoriented, unable to determine which direction was up."
  - line: 293
    type: narration
    text: "He crashed into sand with impact that would have shattered human bones but merely knocked wind from lungs and dignity from spirit."
  - line: 295
    type: narration
    text: "Never doing that again, Zaron muttered."
  - line: 297
    type: narration
    text: "Agreed, from Applicator."
  - line: 299
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"AGREED,\""
  - line: 300
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt gasped, pulling himself upright and immediately throwing up telekinetic shield as energy bolts converged on his position."
  - line: 302
    type: narration
    text: "The Federation enforcers pressed their advantage—coordinated assault from multiple angles, weapons set to stun rather than kill because they still wanted the armor intact, still prioritized confiscation over elimination despite \"extreme prejudice\" authorization."
  - line: 304
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt fought with everything three consciousnesses could muster—telekinesis creating barriers and projectiles, armor providing strength beyond human norm, tactical analysis suggesting optimal responses even as adolescent fear threatened to overwhelm coordination."
  - line: 306
    type: narration
    text: "But he was losing."
  - line: 307
    type: narration
    text: "Slowly."
  - line: 308
    type: narration
    text: "Incrementally."
  - line: 309
    type: narration
    text: "Six professional enforcers against one former slave with unreliable god-armor was mathematics that didn't favor underdog regardless of narrative preference."
  - line: 311
    type: narration
    text: "Then—reinforcement."
  - line: 313
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck emerged from the compound like living tank, scales gleaming in doubled sunlight, moving with purpose that suggested he'd ensured freed slaves were safe and now returned to what he did best—combat that made use of size and strength and centuries of military experience."
  - line: 315
    type: narration
    text: "The reptilian didn't announce himself, didn't offer warning—simply grabbed nearest Federation enforcer and used it as improvised weapon against two others, massive strength turning bureaucrats into projectiles."
  - line: 317
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Oreck
    text: "\"Thought you might need backup,\""
  - line: 319
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Appreciated!\""
  - line: 320
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt managed, using moment of distraction to channel telekinetic force against crystalline being—not trying to harm but to separate, to create space, to prevent overwhelming numerical advantage from deciding engagement through simple attrition."
  - line: 322
    type: narration
    text: "The battle shifted—two against six was still disadvantageous but within realm of possibility, especially when one combatant was massive reptilian with centuries of experience and other was wearing armor that, despite adolescent unpredictability, still represented Aeon Keeper technology beyond Federation standard equipment."
  - line: 324
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara observed from distance, white eyes showing first hint of something beyond cold assessment—perhaps concern, perhaps calculation, perhaps recognition that enforcement operation had become significantly more complicated than initial briefing suggested."
  - line: 326
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Enforcer Vel'thara,\""
  - line: 327
    type: narration
    text: "the crystalline being called out, voice chiming through combat chaos. \"Subject Geralt demonstrates capabilities exceeding preliminary assessment. Armor functionality suggests consciousness integration rather than simple wearing. Recommend revised approach—\""
  - line: 329
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Negative,\""
  - line: 330
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara interrupted. \"Protocols are clear. Unauthorized artifacts must be confiscated. Hostile subjects must be neutralized. Continue engagement.\""
  - line: 332
    type: narration
    text: "But its tone carried less certainty than before—first crack in absolute authority, first suggestion that perhaps galactic law enforcement wasn't prepared for former slave who'd bonded with fragmented god and refused to hide behind mask."
  - line: 334
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt pressed the advantage—not trying to kill because despite everything, these were beings following orders rather than choosing cruelty, were enforcers of unjust system rather than architects of oppression itself."
  - line: 336
    type: narration
    text: "But he would stop them."
  - line: 337
    type: narration
    text: "Would prevent confiscation."
  - line: 338
    type: narration
    text: "Would ensure they understood that Earth's liberation wasn't negotiable regardless of cosmic regulations."
  - line: 340
    type: narration
    text: "He channeled telekinesis in patterns the Applicator suggested, creating sand vortex that surrounded Federation enforcers, that limited visibility and mobility, that forced them to fight defensively rather than pressing coordinated assault."
  - line: 342
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck used the distraction to grab two enforcers simultaneously—one in each massive hand—and simply held them, preventing their weapons from targeting while making clear that crushing them was option he'd chosen not to exercise."
  - line: 344
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Surrender,\""
  - line: 345
    type: narration
    text: "the reptilian said quietly, speaking to beings he held captive. \"This doesn't have to end in death. Withdraw. Report that enforcement failed. Let your superiors decide if escalation is worth the cost.\""
  - line: 347
    type: narration
    text: "The shadow-being appeared behind Oreck—weapon raised, energy blade positioned to strike at exposed spine—"
  - line: 349
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's telekinetic force caught it mid-swing, yanked it away from Oreck's back, and slammed it into sand with enough force to stun but not kill."
  - line: 351
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"We're not trying to hurt you,\""
  - line: 353
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara's white eyes showed something that might have been respect or might have been calculation of how much paperwork failed enforcement operation would generate."
  - line: 355
    type: narration
    text: "Then decision crystallized across features carved from living obsidian:"
  - line: 357
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Operation parameters exceeded. Threat level confirms subject Geralt—designation RAGNAROK—requires specialized response beyond standard enforcement capability. Recommend orbital support and tactical reassessment.\""
  - line: 359
    type: narration
    text: "It raised hand—signal that caused other Federation enforcers to disengage immediately, to fall back toward their ship with discipline that spoke to training that valued survival over pride."
  - line: 361
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"This engagement concludes,\""
  - line: 362
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara announced, addressing Geralt directly. \"But understand—you are now flagged across every Federation database. Your identity is recorded. Your face is captured. The armor's signature is cataloged. Designation RAGNAROK will follow you for remainder of your existence.\""
  - line: 364
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Every bounty hunter seeking profit. Every enforcer pursuing advancement. Every Anunnaki wanting revenge. They will all know exactly who you are and what you've done.\""
  - line: 366
    type: narration
    text: "Vel'thara paused at the ship's ramp, white eyes meeting Geralt's gaze with weight that transcended simple threat."
  - line: 368
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You chose to show your face. To claim responsibility openly. To reject anonymity that might have granted safety. That choice will define everything that follows.\""
  - line: 370
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"I know,\""
  - line: 372
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Perhaps you should.\""
  - line: 373
    type: narration
    text: "The enforcer's tone carried something approaching warning that might have been professional courtesy between adversaries. \"The galaxy is vast. The Federation is patient. And Ragnarok—the end of worlds—is designation that invites response far beyond what you've experienced today.\""
  - line: 375
    type: narration
    text: "The ship's ramp sealed."
  - line: 376
    type: narration
    text: "Engines ignited."
  - line: 377
    type: narration
    text: "And within moments, the Federation vessel ascended—leaving behind churned sand and scattered glass sculptures and former slave who'd just been declared enemy of galactic order."
  - line: 379
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck released the two enforcers he'd been holding—both staggering toward their departing ship, barely making it aboard before ramp sealed and ascent began."
  - line: 381
    type: narration
    text: "Silence settled over the compound—broken only by wind and the distant sound of freed slaves emerging from cover, checking for casualties, processing what they'd witnessed."
  - line: 383
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood motionless, armor settling around him as Zaron's consciousness relaxed from combat readiness, as the Applicator compiled damage assessments and tactical analysis, as his own awareness tried to comprehend what he'd just accepted."
  - line: 385
    type: narration
    text: "We're marked now, Zaron observed quietly."
  - line: 386
    type: narration
    text: "They know who we are."
  - line: 387
    type: narration
    text: "What we are."
  - line: 388
    type: narration
    text: "They'll never stop hunting."
  - line: 390
    type: narration
    text: "Correct, the Applicator confirmed."
  - line: 391
    type: narration
    text: "Federation efficiency at information distribution is formidable."
  - line: 392
    type: narration
    text: "Within hours, every major system will have your identity flagged."
  - line: 393
    type: narration
    text: "Within days, bounty notices will circulate through criminal networks."
  - line: 394
    type: narration
    text: "Within weeks, specialized hunters will begin tracking."
  - line: 396
    type: narration
    text: "The anonymity we might have maintained is permanently sacrificed."
  - line: 398
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"I know,\""
  - line: 400
    type: narration
    text: "He looked at the compound—at freed slaves who'd witnessed confrontation, who'd seen him fight Federation enforcement, who understood that consequences would extend beyond single engagement."
  - line: 402
    type: narration
    text: "Mika approached slowly, hands forming careful gestures before remembering she could speak:"
  - line: 404
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"They called you Ragnarok. They said you're the end of worlds. What does that mean?\""
  - line: 406
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt met her gaze—human looking at human, former slave looking at former slave, both understanding that freedom demanded prices that went beyond simple survival."
  - line: 408
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"It means,\""
  - line: 410
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"It means they'll hunt me. Forever. Across every system. Through every generation. The name Ragnarok will outlive me, will attach to anyone who wears this armor, will become legend that transcends individual existence.\""
  - line: 412
    type: narration
    text: "He paused, feeling the weight of what he'd accepted, of choice that couldn't be unmade."
  - line: 414
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"But also—it means they're afraid. That showing my face, claiming responsibility, refusing to hide behind mask made them understand we're not just lucky slaves who got fortunate. We're people who chose liberation and will defend that choice against anything they send.\""
  - line: 416
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And that terrifies them more than any weapon.\""
  - line: 418
    type: narration
    text: "The Five emerged from the compound—constellation still intact, loyal despite trauma, committed despite inability to accept all gifts offered."
  - line: 419
    type: narration
    text: "Jin's hands formed careful gestures:"
  - line: 421
    type: narration
    text: "You-chose, face-exposed, forever-hunted."
  - line: 422
    type: narration
    text: "Why-no-hide?"
  - line: 424
    type: narration
    text: "(You chose to expose your face, accepting eternal pursuit."
  - line: 425
    type: narration
    text: "Why didn't you hide?)"
  - line: 427
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt looked at Jin—at being who understood consequences of modification, who maintained boundaries despite loyalty, who demonstrated that commitment didn't require absolute trust."
  - line: 429
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Because hiding would mean accepting shame. Would mean believing freedom is something to apologize for rather than celebrate. Would mean letting them define me through fear rather than defining myself through choice.\""
  - line: 431
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'm Geralt. I freed you. I claimed this armor. I killed the Overseer. Those are facts, not crimes. And I won't pretend otherwise just because they decided liberation violates their precious regulations.\""
  - line: 433
    type: narration
    text: "Jin's expression shifted—something approaching approval crossing features that usually showed only careful neutrality."
  - line: 434
    type: narration
    text: "His hands formed single gesture:"
  - line: 436
    type: narration
    text: "Worthy-of-armor."
  - line: 437
    type: narration
    text: "Worthy-of-trust."
  - line: 439
    type: narration
    text: "Coming from Jin—from one who'd learned trust was dangerous, who maintained protective distance despite loyalty—the acknowledgment carried weight that transcended simple approval."
  - line: 441
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck approached from where he'd been checking perimeter, ensuring no Federation surveillance remained active."
  - line: 443
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"They'll be back,\""
  - line: 444
    type: narration
    text: "the reptilian said quietly. \"Not tomorrow. Not next week. But eventually. With better preparation. With specialized equipment. With authorization to use lethal force if necessary.\""
  - line: 446
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know.\""
  - line: 448
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And they'll bring others. Bounty hunters. Anunnaki seeking revenge. Anyone who sees profit or advancement in claiming Ragnarok's head.\""
  - line: 450
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know.\""
  - line: 452
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Your life just became significantly more complicated.\""
  - line: 454
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I KNOW.\""
  - line: 455
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt frustration bleeding into his tone—not at Oreck, but at situation that offered no good options, only graduated scales of consequence. \"But what was I supposed to do? Hide? Let them take the armor? Surrender to processing and hope they'd treat former slave with compassion?\""
  - line: 457
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Oreck
    text: "\"No,\""
  - line: 459
    type: narration
    text: "He placed massive clawed hand on Geralt's armored shoulder—gesture that bridged species differences and circumstantial chasms."
  - line: 461
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"But understand—this was easy. Six enforcers with non-lethal priorities. Next time will be harder. The time after that, harder still. They'll keep escalating until they either succeed in confiscating the armor or decide you're not worth the resources required for capture.\""
  - line: 463
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And that decision,\""
  - line: 464
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck continued with tone that carried centuries of military experience, \"will only come after they've thrown everything they have at you and found it insufficient. You've started war that won't end until either you're dead or they've accepted that some things can't be controlled through cosmic law.\""
  - line: 466
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt looked at the armor encasing him—at scales that gleamed in doubled sunlight, at technology that represented sacrifice and choice and consciousness willing to fragment itself for purposes that transcended individual existence."
  - line: 468
    type: narration
    text: "We knew this was possible, Zaron said quietly."
  - line: 469
    type: narration
    text: "When I chose to become weapon rather than observer."
  - line: 470
    type: narration
    text: "When I fragmented myself and bound consciousness to metal."
  - line: 471
    type: narration
    text: "I knew wearing me would make host target."
  - line: 472
    type: narration
    text: "That becoming actor meant becoming noticed."
  - line: 474
    type: narration
    text: "You accepted that burden knowingly."
  - line: 475
    type: narration
    text: "Don't regret it now."
  - line: 477
    type: narration
    text: "Tactical assessment suggests multiple response strategies, the Applicator added with characteristic precision."
  - line: 478
    type: narration
    text: "We can remain mobile, avoid detection, minimize exposure."
  - line: 479
    type: narration
    text: "Or we can embrace visibility, use reputation as weapon, force them to commit resources that might otherwise be deployed against less defended populations."
  - line: 481
    type: narration
    text: "Both approaches have merit."
  - line: 482
    type: narration
    text: "But hiding after this seems... inconsistent with established behavioral patterns."
  - line: 484
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"You're right,\""
  - line: 486
    type: narration
    text: "He addressed the compound—three hundred freed slaves, five silent witnesses, one reptilian ally who'd chosen redemption over conditioning:"
  - line: 488
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"They called me Ragnarok. The end of worlds. The twilight of gods. They meant it as designation—threat classification to justify extreme response.\""
  - line: 490
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"But I'm claiming it as identity. As purpose. As promise that their world—their cosmic order built on enslavement and extraction and regulations that enable atrocity—is ending. One compound at a time. One liberated population at a time. One defiant choice at a time.\""
  - line: 492
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We're not just freed slaves anymore. We're proof that resistance works. We're demonstration that cosmic law can be defied. We're the beginning of something they can't stop through enforcement operations or threat classifications.\""
  - line: 494
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We're Ragnarok. And worlds that enslave conscious beings deserve to end.\""
  - line: 496
    type: narration
    text: "The compound erupted in sound—voices newly granted raised in affirmation, gesture-language forming cascades of agreement, recognition that they'd crossed threshold that couldn't be uncrossed."
  - line: 498
    type: narration
    text: "They weren't hiding anymore."
  - line: 500
    type: narration
    text: "They weren't asking permission anymore."
  - line: 502
    type: narration
    text: "They were declaring war on galaxy that viewed them as resources rather than people."
  - line: 504
    type: narration
    text: "And Geralt—human wearing god-consciousness, trinity of awareness unified in purpose despite constant disagreement, former slave who'd claimed identity through choice rather than accepting designation—stood at the center of it all."
  - line: 506
    type: narration
    text: "Marked."
  - line: 507
    type: narration
    text: "Hunted."
  - line: 508
    type: narration
    text: "Identified."
  - line: 510
    type: narration
    text: "Ragnarok."
  - line: 512
    type: narration
    text: "The Federation ship disappeared into atmosphere, carrying recordings and assessments and warnings that would propagate through every major system within days."
  - line: 514
    type: narration
    text: "The twin suns descended toward horizon, painting compound in shades of crimson that suggested either sunset or prophecy."
  - line: 516
    type: narration
    text: "And somewhere in the galaxy's vast bureaucratic network, databases were updating with new designation:"
  - line: 518
    type: narration
    text: "SUBJECT: RAGNAROK (Primary Identity: Geralt)"
  - line: 519
    type: narration
    text: "SPECIES: Human (Earth Origin)"
  - line: 520
    type: narration
    text: "CRIMES: Unauthorized Aeon Keeper Artifact Possession, Assault on Federation Personnel, Inciting Rebellion, Genetic Modification Without Authorization"
  - line: 521
    type: narration
    text: "STATUS: ACTIVE THREAT - TERMINATE OR CAPTURE"
  - line: 522
    type: narration
    text: "BOUNTY: MAXIMUM"
  - line: 523
    type: narration
    text: "NOTES: Subject refuses concealment."
  - line: 524
    type: narration
    text: "Face recorded."
  - line: 525
    type: narration
    text: "Identity confirmed."
  - line: 526
    type: narration
    text: "Dragon Mail bonded at soul level—confiscation may require subject termination."
  - line: 527
    type: narration
    text: "Approach with extreme caution."
  - line: 528
    type: narration
    text: "Designation \"Ragnarok\" reflects assessed threat to cosmic order."
  - line: 530
    type: narration
    text: "The war for Earth's liberation had begun with single slave stopping whip."
  - line: 532
    type: narration
    text: "It escalated with compound freed through desperate courage."
  - line: 534
    type: narration
    text: "And now—now it became legend that would span millennia, that would attach to armor rather than individual, that would make \"Ragnarok\" designation that outlived any single wearer."
  - line: 536
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt had chosen visibility over safety."
  - line: 538
    type: narration
    text: "Identity over anonymity."
  - line: 540
    type: narration
    text: "Defiance over survival."
  - line: 542
    type: narration
    text: "And the galaxy would learn—slowly, painfully, through battles and liberations and defeats and victories that stretched across decades—that some choices mattered more than consequences."
  - line: 544
    type: narration
    text: "That freedom was worth any price."
  - line: 546
    type: narration
    text: "That cosmic order built on enslavement deserved to end."
  - line: 548
    type: narration
    text: "Tomorrow, they would begin planning the first campaign."
  - line: 549
    type: narration
    text: "The first intentional liberation."
  - line: 550
    type: narration
    text: "The first demonstration that what happened at this compound could be replicated, could spread, could become movement rather than isolated incident."
  - line: 552
    type: narration
    text: "But tonight—tonight they celebrated."
  - line: 553
    type: narration
    text: "Not victory, because the war had only just begun."
  - line: 554
    type: narration
    text: "But choice."
  - line: 555
    type: narration
    text: "Identity."
  - line: 556
    type: narration
    text: "The claiming of designation that was meant as threat but became promise."
  - line: 558
    type: narration
    text: "They were Ragnarok."
  - line: 560
    type: narration
    text: "And the twilight of gods had arrived."
  - line: 563
    type: narration
    text: "The Infiltration"
  - line: 565
    type: narration
    text: "The second compound lay three days' march northeast of their liberated territory—close enough to reach with minimal supply requirements, far enough that Anunnaki communication between facilities had been limited to monthly status reports rather than daily coordination."
  - line: 566
    type: narration
    text: "That isolation made it ideal target."
  - line: 567
    type: narration
    text: "Vulnerable."
  - line: 568
    type: narration
    text: "Unwarned."
  - line: 569
    type: narration
    text: "Still operating under assumption that cosmic order remained intact and slaves remained compliant."
  - line: 571
    type: narration
    text: "They were about to learn otherwise."
  - line: 573
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt studied the compound from distance—using magnification capabilities the Applicator could provide through interface with his optic nerve, seeing details that unaided human vision couldn't distinguish."
  - line: 574
    type: narration
    text: "The layout was nearly identical to their own former prison."
  - line: 575
    type: narration
    text: "Same architectural design."
  - line: 576
    type: narration
    text: "Same defensive positions."
  - line: 577
    type: narration
    text: "Same assumption that slaves required containment rather than fortification against external threat."
  - line: 579
    type: narration
    text: "The Anunnaki didn't build walls to keep enemies out."
  - line: 580
    type: narration
    text: "They built them to keep property in."
  - line: 582
    type: narration
    text: "That assumption was about to cost them everything."
  - line: 584
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Fifteen visible guards,\""
  - line: 585
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt reported to the assembled strike team—twenty volunteers from their compound, chosen for capability and commitment rather than simple willingness. \"One Overseer, based on the golden sheen visible in the central structure. Standard patrol patterns, rotating every four hours. No indication they're aware we're coming.\""
  - line: 587
    type: narration
    text: "Mika crouched beside him, studying the compound with tactical awareness that had developed rapidly over past weeks."
  - line: 588
    type: narration
    text: "Her voice—still rough but growing more confident with use—carried the certainty of someone who'd transformed from victim to warrior through choice rather than conscription."
  - line: 590
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The slaves. How many?\""
  - line: 592
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Approximately two hundred based on dormitory size. Same modifications we had—no speech, limited cognitive enhancement, conditioned for obedience through genetic and psychological manipulation.\""
  - line: 594
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Will they fight for us?\""
  - line: 596
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Unknown,\""
  - line: 597
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt admitted. \"They don't know liberation is possible. Don't know resistance can succeed. Don't know we exist.\""
  - line: 599
    type: narration
    text: "He turned to face Mika directly."
  - line: 601
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"That's why you're going in first. You and the others. You look like slaves because you were slaves. You still bear the scars, the modifications, the physical markers that identify you as property rather than people. You can blend in. Get close. Position yourselves.\""
  - line: 603
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And when you give the signal?\""
  - line: 605
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You attack. Before the Anunnaki even realize we're there. Before they can coordinate defense. You'll have maybe thirty seconds of complete surprise before they understand what's happening.\""
  - line: 607
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's expression showed understanding—and acceptance of risk that came with being first through the breach, with striking from inside while wearing skin of those still enslaved."
  - line: 609
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And you?\""
  - line: 611
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt smiled—expression that carried confidence some might call arrogance but he considered realistic assessment of capabilities armor provided."
  - line: 613
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'm going to walk up to the front gate and introduce myself. Very politely. Very obviously. While they're focused on the terrifying armored figure demanding entry, you'll already be inside. Waiting.\""
  - line: 615
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck approached from where he'd been checking equipment with strike team—massive reptilian presence that drew eyes despite weeks of acclimation to his alliance."
  - line: 617
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"I'll position at the rear entrance,\""
  - line: 619
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Three-point assault,\""
  - line: 620
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt confirmed. \"Mika's team from inside, me from front, you from rear. By the time the Overseer understands what's happening, his forces will already be disabled and he'll be facing three-way convergence with no retreat options.\""
  - line: 622
    type: narration
    text: "He looked at the volunteers—twenty beings who'd chosen to risk liberation they'd achieved to grant it to others still enslaved."
  - line: 623
    type: narration
    text: "Mika and five others would infiltrate."
  - line: 624
    type: narration
    text: "The remaining fourteen would accompany Oreck, ready to pour through rear breach once he'd created opening."
  - line: 626
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"This is real combat,\""
  - line: 628
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Some of you might die. Some of the slaves we're trying to free might die. Success isn't guaranteed just because our cause is righteous.\""
  - line: 630
    type: narration
    text: "He paused, giving weight to words that needed to land with full impact."
  - line: 632
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"If anyone wants to withdraw, do it now. No shame. No judgment. Choosing to protect what we've already achieved rather than risking it for strangers is valid decision.\""
  - line: 634
    type: narration
    text: "None moved."
  - line: 635
    type: narration
    text: "None spoke."
  - line: 636
    type: narration
    text: "None even gestured doubt."
  - line: 638
    type: narration
    text: "Finally, one of the volunteers—young male who'd claimed name \"Dren\" after receiving speech—broke silence:"
  - line: 640
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We were those strangers once. Someone had to risk everything to free us. Now it's our turn to be that someone for others.\""
  - line: 642
    type: narration
    text: "Murmured agreement rippled through the group—recognition that liberation was responsibility not just privilege, that freedom demanded eternal vigilance and willingness to extend it to those still enslaved."
  - line: 644
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"Then we move,\""
  - line: 646
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Oreck and assault team hold at rear breach point. Wait for signal.\""
  - line: 648
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I approach front gate at midday. Maximum visibility. Maximum intimidation. Draw every eye to me while you work from inside.\""
  - line: 650
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"When I break down the gate—that's your signal. That's when chaos begins. Hit fast, hit hard, and don't give them time to coordinate response.\""
  - line: 652
    type: narration
    text: "He looked at compound in the distance—at another prison wearing architecture's skin, at another population living under assumption that resistance was impossible and liberation was fantasy."
  - line: 654
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We're going to teach them otherwise. We're going to demonstrate that what happened at our compound wasn't miracle—it was choice. Pattern that can be replicated. Movement that spreads faster than Anunnaki can respond.\""
  - line: 656
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We're going to free them. And then we're going to do it again. And again. Until Earth has no compounds left, no slaves remaining, no populations accepting enslavement as natural order.\""
  - line: 658
    type: narration
    text: "Host, the Applicator stirred with tone that carried both pride and concern."
  - line: 659
    type: narration
    text: "This is significant strategic evolution."
  - line: 660
    type: narration
    text: "From defensive operations to offensive campaigns."
  - line: 661
    type: narration
    text: "From protecting liberation achieved to extending liberation to others."
  - line: 662
    type: narration
    text: "The tactical implications are—"
  - line: 664
    type: narration
    text: "Terrifying and exhilarating, Zaron interrupted."
  - line: 665
    type: narration
    text: "This is what I sacrificed everything for."
  - line: 666
    type: narration
    text: "Not just to protect single compound but to become weapon that could challenge empire."
  - line: 667
    type: narration
    text: "That could demonstrate that even cosmic order can be defied through choice and courage."
  - line: 669
    type: narration
    text: "Try not to get us killed, Geralt thought to both of them."
  - line: 670
    type: narration
    text: "Confidence is good."
  - line: 671
    type: narration
    text: "Overconfidence gets everyone dead."
  - line: 673
    type: narration
    text: "The team dispersed—Mika's infiltration group moving to staging area where they'd wait for dawn, Oreck's assault team checking equipment and reviewing breach protocols, others returning to main compound to ensure defensive positions remained manned despite offensive operation."
  - line: 675
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt remained at observation point, watching the compound in distance, feeling the armor settle around him with increasing comfort as Zaron learned his patterns and the Applicator refined interface protocols."
  - line: 677
    type: narration
    text: "Tomorrow, they'd discover if liberation could be taught."
  - line: 678
    type: narration
    text: "If freedom could be shared."
  - line: 679
    type: narration
    text: "If what they'd achieved through desperate defense could be replicated through deliberate attack."
  - line: 681
    type: narration
    text: "Tomorrow, the war for Earth escalated from survival to campaign."
  - line: 683
    type: narration
    text: "Tomorrow, they'd learn if Ragnarok was designation that inspired fear because it represented genuine threat or simply because Federation bureaucrats enjoyed dramatic classifications."
  - line: 685
    type: narration
    text: "The twin suns set, painting the desert in shades that suggested either blood or promise depending on observer's temperament."
  - line: 687
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt chose promise."
  - line: 689
    type: narration
    text: "After all—tomorrow's battle wasn't about destroying enemies."
  - line: 690
    type: narration
    text: "It was about freeing people."
  - line: 692
    type: narration
    text: "And that cause was worth any risk."
  - line: 694
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 696
    type: narration
    text: "The Approach"
  - line: 698
    type: narration
    text: "Dawn broke over the compound with light that suggested normalcy—another day in endless series, another rotation of labor and compliance, another confirmation that cosmic order remained intact and slaves remained property rather than people."
  - line: 700
    type: narration
    text: "Mika led her infiltration team toward mining operations that extended beyond compound walls—work parties supervised by single guard rather than full security detail, vulnerability that existed because Anunnaki had never conceived that slaves might coordinate resistance across compounds."
  - line: 702
    type: narration
    text: "They looked like what they were—scarred, modified, bearing physical markers of enslavement that made them indistinguishable from the two hundred beings already laboring under Anunnaki authority."
  - line: 703
    type: narration
    text: "No weapons visible."
  - line: 704
    type: narration
    text: "No signs of coordination."
  - line: 705
    type: narration
    text: "Just another group of property performing assigned functions."
  - line: 707
    type: narration
    text: "The guard barely glanced at them—vertical pupils registering presence but not threat, consciousness that had spent decades viewing slaves as objects incapable of defiance."
  - line: 708
    type: narration
    text: "Conditioning that was about to prove fatal."
  - line: 710
    type: narration
    text: "Mika and her team integrated with existing work parties, moving with practiced subservience that hid awareness and capability beneath mask of compliance."
  - line: 711
    type: narration
    text: "They'd spent weeks learning to weaponize the Anunnaki's expectations, to use assumptions about slave incapability as tactical advantage."
  - line: 713
    type: narration
    text: "One team member \"accidentally\" stumbled near guard post, creating distraction while another palmed crude weapon from concealed location."
  - line: 714
    type: narration
    text: "Another engaged overseer in gesture-language about work quotas, buying seconds for positioning that placed infiltrators near critical chokepoints."
  - line: 716
    type: narration
    text: "By midmorning, Mika's team was distributed throughout the compound—six beings positioned near weapon storage, guard posts, communication systems, and the central structure where Overseer coordinated operations."
  - line: 718
    type: narration
    text: "None of the enslaved population recognized them as outsiders."
  - line: 719
    type: narration
    text: "The guards noticed nothing unusual."
  - line: 720
    type: narration
    text: "Even the Overseer—visible occasionally through windows that showed golden flesh coordinating daily operations—remained unaware that his compound had already been compromised from within."
  - line: 722
    type: narration
    text: "Mika checked positions through subtle gestures that looked like normal slave communication—confirmation that everyone was ready, that weapons were acquired, that chaos could be unleashed on signal."
  - line: 724
    type: narration
    text: "Now they waited."
  - line: 726
    type: narration
    text: "For the armored figure who would draw every eye while they struck from shadows."
  - line: 728
    type: narration
    text: "For Ragnarok to announce himself."
  - line: 730
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 732
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck positioned his assault team at the compound's rear boundary—fourteen volunteers spread along wall that separated facility from desert beyond, concealed behind rock formations and elevation changes that provided cover from casual observation."
  - line: 734
    type: narration
    text: "The reptilian studied the wall with tactical assessment honed through centuries—identifying weakest points, calculating optimal breach locations, preparing to move with speed that would transform defensive barrier into open pathway within seconds of engagement beginning."
  - line: 736
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"Remember,\""
  - line: 738
    type: narration
    text: "Dren—young volunteer who'd spoken so eloquently about responsibility—nodded understanding while checking crude club he'd fashioned from salvaged materials."
  - line: 740
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And the Overseer?\""
  - line: 742
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Oreck
    text: "\"Geralt handles the Overseer,\""
  - line: 744
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Our job is everyone else. The guards, the slave drivers, anyone who tries to interfere with liberation. We're the hammer that compresses their forces toward the center where Geralt will be waiting.\""
  - line: 746
    type: narration
    text: "He checked the sun's position—approaching zenith, time when shadows were minimal and visibility maximized."
  - line: 747
    type: narration
    text: "When armored figure approaching from open desert would be impossible to miss."
  - line: 749
    type: narration
    text: "When Ragnarok would introduce himself to beings who'd never heard the designation, who didn't know liberation was spreading like fire through compounds that had seemed eternal."
  - line: 751
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Soon,\""
  - line: 752
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck muttered. \"Very soon now.\""
  - line: 754
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 756
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt walked."
  - line: 758
    type: narration
    text: "Not with stealth."
  - line: 759
    type: narration
    text: "Not with tactical awareness of cover and concealment."
  - line: 760
    type: narration
    text: "Not with anything approaching military discipline."
  - line: 762
    type: narration
    text: "He simply walked up the main approach to the compound's front gate like he was visiting rather than attacking, like he had every right to be there, like the armor encasing him was normal rather than technology that screamed Aeon Keeper origin."
  - line: 764
    type: narration
    text: "The Dragon Mail gleamed in doubled sunlight—scales catching radiance and refracting it in patterns that made him visible from miles away, that announced presence with authority that transcended verbal declaration."
  - line: 765
    type: narration
    text: "Wing-mounts folded but clearly present."
  - line: 766
    type: narration
    text: "Helm retracted, showing his face—human features that marked him as former slave rather than Anunnaki authority, that made his approach even more impossible to process through normal assumptions."
  - line: 768
    type: narration
    text: "They see us, the Applicator noted clinically."
  - line: 769
    type: narration
    text: "Guard posts activating."
  - line: 770
    type: narration
    text: "Alert protocols engaging."
  - line: 771
    type: narration
    text: "Overseer being notified."
  - line: 773
    type: narration
    text: "Good, Zaron said with satisfaction that bordered on anticipation."
  - line: 774
    type: narration
    text: "Let them see."
  - line: 775
    type: narration
    text: "Let them wonder."
  - line: 776
    type: narration
    text: "Let them try to understand why former slave approaches wearing technology they can't comprehend."
  - line: 778
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt the armor settle around him with confidence that had been building over weeks of practice—Zaron learning to trust his judgment, the Applicator refining tactical suggestions rather than making demands, three consciousnesses functioning as unified system despite constant internal debate."
  - line: 780
    type: narration
    text: "He reached the gate—massive barrier designed to contain rather than repel, to keep property from escaping rather than keeping enemies from entering."
  - line: 782
    type: narration
    text: "A guard appeared above the wall—reptilian similar to Oreck but smaller, younger, carrying weapon with professional competence but expression mixing confusion with concern."
  - line: 784
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Halt,\""
  - line: 785
    type: narration
    text: "the guard called out in Anunnaki dialect that Geralt's newly restored speech allowed him to comprehend. \"Identify yourself. State your business. This is authorized Anunnaki facility operating under—\""
  - line: 787
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I am Geralt,\""
  - line: 788
    type: narration
    text: "he interrupted, voice amplified by armor's systems to carry across compound. \"Also known as Ragnarok. Also known as the slave who killed his Overseer and freed his compound and claimed armor the Aeon Keepers prepared for exactly this purpose.\""
  - line: 790
    type: narration
    text: "He gestured casually at the gate between them—scales gleaming, power radiating with intensity that made air itself shimmer."
  - line: 792
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'm here to liberate your compound. To free the slaves you call property. To kill your Overseer and demonstrate that cosmic order is negotiable rather than absolute.\""
  - line: 794
    type: narration
    text: "The guard stared—incomprehension warring with recognition that something fundamental had shifted, that assumptions about slave compliance were being directly challenged by being who should have been cowering rather than confronting."
  - line: 796
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You...\""
  - line: 797
    type: narration
    text: "the guard managed, \"you're insane. One slave against entire compound? Against Overseer blessed by Anu himself? Against guard force trained for—\""
  - line: 799
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Correction,\""
  - line: 800
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt interrupted again, allowing small smile to cross his features. \"Not one slave. An organized liberation force. Some of whom are already inside your compound. Waiting.\""
  - line: 802
    type: narration
    text: "He raised his hand—armored gauntlet catching light with dramatic flair that Zaron provided despite Geralt's eye-roll at the theatrical addition."
  - line: 804
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Last chance. Open the gate. Release the slaves. Withdraw peacefully. Live to tell Federation enforcement that some fights aren't worth the casualties.\""
  - line: 806
    type: narration
    text: "The guard's expression hardened—confusion giving way to determination born of centuries of conditioning, of training that said Anunnaki authority was absolute and slave resistance was impossible."
  - line: 808
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We will never—\""
  - line: 810
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt didn't let him finish."
  - line: 812
    type: narration
    text: "He channeled telekinetic force through the armor—the Applicator amplifying power, Zaron providing animation that made gesture more dramatic than necessary, his own will directing energy toward gate that had never been designed to withstand assault from outside."
  - line: 814
    type: narration
    text: "The gate exploded inward—metal shrieking, stone cracking, barrier that had contained property for decades suddenly becoming scattered debris and open pathway."
  - line: 816
    type: narration
    text: "The signal had been given."
  - line: 818
    type: narration
    text: "Inside the compound, Mika and her team struck."
  - line: 820
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 822
    type: narration
    text: "The Chaos"
  - line: 824
    type: narration
    text: "The infiltrators moved with synchronization that came from weeks of training—six beings acting as unified force despite physical separation, coordinating through gesture-language and shared understanding of tactical objectives."
  - line: 826
    type: narration
    text: "Weapon storage was compromised first—guard positioned there collapsing as crude club connected with skull, keys acquired, energy weapons distributed to slaves who'd only ever held mining equipment suddenly grasping technology that could punch through armor or vaporize targets."
  - line: 828
    type: narration
    text: "Communication systems went dark—crystalline relay that connected compound to Anunnaki network shattered through telekinetic force that Mika had been developing, that remained crude compared to Geralt's capability but sufficient for sabotage."
  - line: 830
    type: narration
    text: "Guard posts erupted in confusion—beings trained to watch for external threat suddenly facing attacks from directions they'd never anticipated, from slaves who should have been compliant suddenly demonstrating coordination and capability that violated every assumption about property's limitations."
  - line: 832
    type: narration
    text: "By the time Geralt's telekinetic explosion announced external assault, half the compound's guard force was already disabled or scrambling to understand attacks from inside."
  - line: 834
    type: narration
    text: "The enslaved population—two hundred beings who'd lived under assumption that resistance was impossible—watched with expressions mixing shock and desperate hope as their world inverted, as slaves became liberators and guards became victims."
  - line: 836
    type: narration
    text: "Some remained frozen by conditioning too deep to overcome through mere observation."
  - line: 837
    type: narration
    text: "Others began moving toward the fighting—not attacking but positioning, preparing, waiting to see if freedom was real or simply new form of torment designed to crush hope more thoroughly than simple oppression."
  - line: 839
    type: narration
    text: "Through the shattered gate, Geralt entered—armor moving with confidence that weeks of practice had developed, that made him appear more competent than he felt given how recently the armor had been bonding and trying to flee from combat."
  - line: 841
    type: narration
    text: "Guards converged on his position—seven beings carrying energy weapons, moving with professional coordination that suggested proper military training rather than simple enforcement capability."
  - line: 843
    type: narration
    text: "Energy bolts blazed—Geralt dodged, throwing up telekinetic barriers that deflected most attacks, accepting minor hits on the armor that Zaron's consciousness absorbed and redistributed without allowing damage to reach flesh beneath."
  - line: 845
    type: narration
    text: "He didn't try for elegant combat."
  - line: 846
    type: narration
    text: "Didn't attempt elaborate techniques."
  - line: 847
    type: narration
    text: "Simply channeled power the armor provided—telekinetically grabbing guards and slamming them into walls or each other, creating chaos that prevented coordinated assault, demonstrating that former slave now possessed capability that transcended everything they'd been taught about natural order."
  - line: 849
    type: narration
    text: "From the rear, Oreck breached."
  - line: 851
    type: narration
    text: "The wall exploded outward—not through subtle demolition but through reptilian applying brute force to structural weakness, through centuries of experience knowing exactly where to hit to transform barrier into rubble."
  - line: 853
    type: narration
    text: "Fourteen volunteers poured through—not soldiers but freed slaves who'd chosen to extend liberation to others, who fought with desperation and determination rather than professional discipline."
  - line: 855
    type: narration
    text: "The compound's guard force found themselves caught in three-way convergence—attacks from inside, outside, and rear simultaneously, coordination they couldn't match with training that had never anticipated slave resistance would be possible."
  - line: 857
    type: narration
    text: "Within minutes, the tactical situation became clear:"
  - line: 859
    type: narration
    text: "The guards were losing."
  - line: 861
    type: narration
    text: "Not through superior numbers or better equipment, but through strategic positioning and element of surprise and willingness to fight for cause that transcended simple survival."
  - line: 863
    type: narration
    text: "One guard attempted to flee—Mika's team blocked the exit, weapons acquired from storage giving them capability to enforce containment they'd once been subjected to."
  - line: 865
    type: narration
    text: "Another guard tried to rally defensive formation—Oreck's massive form shattered the attempt, reptilian strength scattering beings like leaves before storm."
  - line: 867
    type: narration
    text: "A third guard raised weapon toward enslaved population—Geralt's telekinetic force caught the being mid-motion, slammed it into ground with enough force to stun but not kill."
  - line: 869
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"SURRENDER,\""
  - line: 870
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's voice boomed across the compound—amplified by armor, carrying authority that transcended simple volume. \"Your forces are disabled. Your Overseer stands alone. This battle is over. Choose survival over pointless resistance.\""
  - line: 872
    type: narration
    text: "Some guards dropped weapons immediately—training versus preservation instinct producing quick calculation that staying alive mattered more than defending abstract authority."
  - line: 874
    type: narration
    text: "Others hesitated—conditioning warring with reality, centuries of belief that Anunnaki supremacy was absolute colliding with evidence that slaves could coordinate, could fight, could WIN."
  - line: 876
    type: narration
    text: "The few who continued fighting were disabled quickly—not through death but through overwhelming force, through being surrounded by beings who'd chosen mercy despite having every reason for vengeance."
  - line: 878
    type: narration
    text: "Within twenty minutes of Geralt breaching the gate, the compound's entire guard force was neutralized."
  - line: 880
    type: narration
    text: "Disabled."
  - line: 881
    type: narration
    text: "Disarmed."
  - line: 882
    type: narration
    text: "Contained."
  - line: 884
    type: narration
    text: "And in the central structure—the Overseer emerged."
  - line: 886
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 888
    type: narration
    text: "The Duel"
  - line: 890
    type: narration
    text: "The Anunnaki Overseer was magnificent—there was no other word adequate to describe being who represented divine authority made manifest, who radiated power that transcended simple physical presence."
  - line: 892
    type: narration
    text: "Twelve feet tall, golden flesh gleaming in doubled sunlight, features that combined humanoid structure with proportions that suggested different evolutionary path, different environmental pressures, different assumptions about what conscious beings should look like."
  - line: 894
    type: narration
    text: "Eyes that weren't eyes—sophisticated sensors that processed information across spectrums human perception couldn't access, that made the Overseer's awareness exceed normal biological limitations."
  - line: 896
    type: narration
    text: "And the voice—when it spoke, reality rippled:"
  - line: 898
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"SLAVE.\""
  - line: 900
    type: narration
    text: "Single word that carried weight of cosmic authority, of millennia of unquestioned supremacy, of genuine confusion that property had somehow acquired capability to challenge ownership."
  - line: 902
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You dare approach this facility? You dare attack authorized Anunnaki operation? You dare claim armor you have no right to possess?\""
  - line: 904
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood in the compound's center—volunteers behind him, guards disabled around him, enslaved population watching from carefully maintained distance."
  - line: 905
    type: narration
    text: "Helm still retracted."
  - line: 906
    type: narration
    text: "Face still visible."
  - line: 907
    type: narration
    text: "Identity still claimed openly despite every tactical reason to hide."
  - line: 909
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"I am Geralt,\""
  - line: 911
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Now I'm here to extend that choice to others still enslaved.\""
  - line: 913
    type: narration
    text: "The Overseer descended from the central structure—each step measured, deliberate, radiating confidence that came from never having experienced genuine threat, from existence where authority was absolute and resistance was impossible."
  - line: 915
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You are aberration. Malfunction. Error that cosmic order will correct. The Federation has designated you Ragnarok—threat requiring elimination. I will claim that distinction. I will present your head to Anu himself as demonstration that even aberrations can be resolved through proper application of force.\""
  - line: 917
    type: narration
    text: "Weapons materialized from the Overseer's form—not carried but integrated, biological and technological merged into systems that made distinction meaningless."
  - line: 918
    type: narration
    text: "Energy projectors that could level buildings."
  - line: 919
    type: narration
    text: "Defensive fields that could deflect projectiles."
  - line: 920
    type: narration
    text: "Combat capability that made individual Anunnaki worth entire military units of lesser species."
  - line: 922
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Last chance,\""
  - line: 923
    type: narration
    text: "the Overseer continued. \"Surrender. Accept that cosmic order is absolute. Die quickly rather than learning through prolonged suffering that gods cannot be defied by property.\""
  - line: 925
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt the armor respond—Zaron's consciousness flooding with readiness that bordered on eagerness, the Applicator providing tactical analysis that suggested dozens of approach vectors and probability assessments, his own will hardening into determination that this being, this representation of everything wrong with cosmic order, would fall."
  - line: 927
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"No,\""
  - line: 929
    type: narration
    text: "He raised his armored hands—scales gleaming, power building, three consciousnesses unified in purpose despite constant internal disagreement."
  - line: 931
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Let's see if gods bleed.\""
  - line: 933
    type: narration
    text: "The Overseer attacked."
  - line: 935
    type: narration
    text: "Energy beams blazed—not crude projectiles but focused particle streams that could vaporize targets or punch through armor depending on intensity selected."
  - line: 936
    type: narration
    text: "The air itself ionized, carrying ozone scent and death promise."
  - line: 938
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt dodged—armor responding with increasing confidence as Zaron learned combat rhythms, as the Applicator provided predictions based on energy signatures, as three consciousnesses began functioning as true unified system."
  - line: 940
    type: narration
    text: "He channeled telekinetic force—not trying to match the Overseer's technological advantage but leveraging capability the Anunnaki couldn't replicate, pulling environment itself into the battle."
  - line: 941
    type: narration
    text: "Sand rose in waves, creating barriers and projectiles."
  - line: 942
    type: narration
    text: "Debris from shattered gate became improvised ammunition."
  - line: 943
    type: narration
    text: "The compound itself became weapon against being who'd built it."
  - line: 945
    type: narration
    text: "The Overseer adjusted tactics—energy projectors shifting from precision strikes to area saturation, trying to overwhelm defensive capability through sheer volume rather than targeted application."
  - line: 947
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt the armor strain—Zaron's consciousness pushed to limits of what adolescent weapon could handle, the Applicator managing power distribution to prevent catastrophic failure, his own flesh beneath scales feeling heat that suggested boundaries were being approached."
  - line: 949
    type: narration
    text: "We need advantage, the Applicator noted clinically."
  - line: 950
    type: narration
    text: "Current trajectory suggests mutual exhaustion rather than decisive victory."
  - line: 951
    type: narration
    text: "Recommend—"
  - line: 953
    type: narration
    text: "I know, Geralt interrupted, seeing the opening, recognizing the pattern in the Overseer's attacks."
  - line: 954
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron, can you give me flight?"
  - line: 955
    type: narration
    text: "Real flight, not panicked ascent?"
  - line: 957
    type: narration
    text: "Maybe?"
  - line: 958
    type: narration
    text: "Zaron said uncertainly."
  - line: 959
    type: narration
    text: "The wings work, I've been practicing while you sleep, but coordinated aerial combat is—"
  - line: 961
    type: narration
    text: "Try."
  - line: 963
    type: narration
    text: "The wings deployed—not randomly this time but deliberately, catching air with precision that suggested Zaron had indeed been practicing, that adolescent armor was maturing faster than any of them had anticipated."
  - line: 965
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt rose—not tumbling but ascending with control that approached grace, that put him above the Overseer's primary firing arcs, that changed three-dimensional combat from ground-based to truly volumetric."
  - line: 967
    type: narration
    text: "From aerial position, he could see the Overseer's defensive fields—energy patterns that surrounded golden flesh with protection that could deflect most attacks."
  - line: 968
    type: narration
    text: "But patterns had gaps."
  - line: 969
    type: narration
    text: "Necessary weaknesses where joints required flexibility, where sensors needed unobstructed access, where even divine technology had to make compromises."
  - line: 971
    type: narration
    text: "He dove—armor responding to intention, wings folding to maximize speed, entire mass becoming projectile that carried force magnified by gravity and acceleration."
  - line: 973
    type: narration
    text: "The Overseer raised defensive fields—energy barriers that should have stopped impact, that should have protected against kinetic assault."
  - line: 975
    type: narration
    text: "But Geralt wasn't relying on kinetic force alone."
  - line: 976
    type: narration
    text: "He channeled telekinesis through the armor—the Applicator amplifying power, Zaron providing animation that made his dive more dramatic than necessary, his own will focusing energy into single point that coincided with gap in defensive fields."
  - line: 978
    type: narration
    text: "Impact."
  - line: 980
    type: narration
    text: "Not with the Overseer's flesh but with the ground beside it—telekinetic force channeling through point of contact to create shockwave that bypassed defensive barriers, that struck from angle the Anunnaki hadn't protected."
  - line: 982
    type: narration
    text: "The Overseer staggered—first sign of vulnerability, first crack in absolute certainty, first suggestion that perhaps cosmic order wasn't as absolute as claimed."
  - line: 984
    type: dialogue
    speaker: it
    text: "\"Impossible,\""
  - line: 986
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"That's your problem,\""
  - line: 987
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt interrupted, pulling himself upright, armor settling around him with confidence that weeks of practice had developed. \"You keep thinking ownership determines capability. That designation defines possibility. That cosmic law reflects natural order rather than constructed hierarchy.\""
  - line: 989
    type: narration
    text: "He channeled more telekinetic force—not attacking directly but pulling the Overseer's weapons systems, interfering with the energy projectors, creating friction in mechanisms that had operated flawlessly for centuries."
  - line: 991
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'm not your property. Not your slave. Not limited by your assumptions about what former slaves can achieve when they choose freedom over compliance.\""
  - line: 993
    type: narration
    text: "The Overseer attempted counterattack—weapons charging despite interference, defensive fields reinforcing, combat systems adapting to recognize that this wasn't aberration that could be dismissed but genuine threat requiring full response."
  - line: 995
    type: narration
    text: "But adaptation took time."
  - line: 996
    type: narration
    text: "And time was resource Geralt had denied through strategic positioning, through coordinated assault from multiple vectors, through being surrounded by allies who'd ensure the Overseer remained focused on single target."
  - line: 998
    type: narration
    text: "Mika and her team positioned at building corners—not attacking but ready, weapons acquired from storage pointed at the Overseer should it try to flee or target enslaved population."
  - line: 1000
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck moved through the compound—ensuring guards remained contained, that casualties were minimized, that liberation remained controlled rather than becoming massacre."
  - line: 1002
    type: narration
    text: "The volunteers watched—bearing witness to confrontation between former slave and divine authority, to demonstration that cosmic order could be defied through choice and courage."
  - line: 1004
    type: narration
    text: "And the enslaved population—two hundred beings who'd lived under assumption that resistance was impossible—watched with expressions transforming from shock to desperate hope to slowly growing certainty that perhaps, perhaps, liberation was real rather than fantasy designed to crush spirits more thoroughly than simple oppression."
  - line: 1006
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt pressed the attack—not trying for elegant combat but recognizing this was demonstration rather than simply tactical engagement, that killing the Overseer mattered less than proving it could be done, that divine authority was negotiable rather than absolute."
  - line: 1008
    type: narration
    text: "He channeled telekinesis in patterns the Applicator suggested—pulling at joints, interfering with sensors, creating cascade failures in systems that had never been designed to withstand concentrated assault from single source."
  - line: 1010
    type: narration
    text: "The Overseer's weapons failed—energy projectors sputtering, defensive fields flickering, combat capability degrading under sustained assault that exceeded design parameters."
  - line: 1012
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"This... this is not...\""
  - line: 1013
    type: narration
    text: "the Overseer struggled to articulate what its consciousness couldn't process. \"You are ERROR. You are MALFUNCTION. You cannot—\""
  - line: 1015
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"I already did,\""
  - line: 1017
    type: narration
    text: "The Overseer collapsed—not dying immediately but wounded beyond ability to continue, consciousness that had never experienced genuine defeat trying to process reality that violated everything it had been taught about natural order."
  - line: 1019
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood over the fallen being—armor gleaming, wings still deployed, face visible to everyone watching."
  - line: 1021
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"Your authority ends here,\""
  - line: 1023
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"It all ends. Now. With choice rather than compliance. With freedom rather than submission. With recognition that consciousness deserves agency regardless of species or origin or designation in your precious hierarchies.\""
  - line: 1025
    type: narration
    text: "He looked at enslaved population—two hundred beings watching, waiting, hoping."
  - line: 1027
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You're free. All of you. Not because I grant freedom but because freedom was always yours. Stolen through modification and conditioning and cultural assumptions, but never truly lost. Just... suppressed. Until someone demonstrated that resistance was possible.\""
  - line: 1029
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Choose for yourselves now. Choose names. Choose voices. Choose lives that transcend designation and property and cosmic regulations.\""
  - line: 1031
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Choose to be people rather than slaves.\""
  - line: 1033
    type: narration
    text: "Silence held for heartbeat."
  - line: 1034
    type: narration
    text: "Two."
  - line: 1035
    type: narration
    text: "Three."
  - line: 1037
    type: narration
    text: "Then—one being stepped forward."
  - line: 1038
    type: narration
    text: "Then another."
  - line: 1039
    type: narration
    text: "Then dozens."
  - line: 1040
    type: narration
    text: "The enslaved population moving toward the fallen Overseer not with violence but with recognition that the being before them no longer represented absolute authority, that divine mandate had limits, that cosmic order could be contested."
  - line: 1042
    type: narration
    text: "Mika approached Geralt—weapon still held but pointed safely away, expression showing pride and exhaustion in equal measure."
  - line: 1044
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The compound is secure,\""
  - line: 1045
    type: narration
    text: "she reported. \"Guards are contained. Casualties minimal—three dead on our side, seven among defenders. Communication systems destroyed. They can't call for help.\""
  - line: 1047
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And the newly freed?\""
  - line: 1049
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Processing. Some are still in shock. Others are already asking questions about how this happened, how we did it, how they can help do it again somewhere else.\""
  - line: 1051
    type: narration
    text: "She paused, smile crossing features scarred by enslavement but illuminated by accomplishment."
  - line: 1053
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Liberation is contagious. You were right about that. It spreads faster than they can contain.\""
  - line: 1055
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt the armor settle around him—Zaron's consciousness pleased with combat performance despite earlier fears, the Applicator compiling tactical data that would improve future operations, his own awareness trying to process that they'd actually done it, that deliberate liberation campaign had succeeded, that proof of concept was complete."
  - line: 1057
    type: narration
    text: "Two compounds freed, Zaron observed."
  - line: 1058
    type: narration
    text: "How many more until Earth is truly liberated?"
  - line: 1060
    type: narration
    text: "Unknown, the Applicator replied."
  - line: 1061
    type: narration
    text: "But each success increases probability of subsequent successes."
  - line: 1062
    type: narration
    text: "Freed slaves become liberators."
  - line: 1063
    type: narration
    text: "Liberators teach tactics."
  - line: 1064
    type: narration
    text: "Tactics spread faster than Anunnaki can adapt."
  - line: 1065
    type: narration
    text: "Momentum builds."
  - line: 1067
    type: narration
    text: "We're not stopping, Geralt thought to both of them."
  - line: 1068
    type: narration
    text: "This was proof that it works."
  - line: 1069
    type: narration
    text: "That liberation can be taught."
  - line: 1070
    type: narration
    text: "That what happened at our compound wasn't miracle—it was pattern that can be replicated."
  - line: 1072
    type: narration
    text: "Two more compounds within marching distance."
  - line: 1073
    type: narration
    text: "Then we expand operations."
  - line: 1074
    type: narration
    text: "Coordinate between liberated facilities."
  - line: 1075
    type: narration
    text: "Build network that transcends single compound."
  - line: 1076
    type: narration
    text: "Create movement that can challenge galactic empire through accumulated choice rather than single dramatic confrontation."
  - line: 1078
    type: narration
    text: "He looked at the fallen Overseer—being who represented everything wrong with cosmic order, who'd viewed conscious beings as property, who'd died confused that slaves could possess capability to challenge authority."
  - line: 1080
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"We're coming for all of them,\""
  - line: 1082
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We're Ragnarok. And your world—your cosmic order built on enslavement—is ending. One liberation at a time.\""
  - line: 1084
    type: narration
    text: "The twin suns descended, painting the newly freed compound in shades that suggested either blood or promise."
  - line: 1086
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt chose promise."
  - line: 1088
    type: narration
    text: "Again."
  - line: 1090
    type: narration
    text: "Always."
  - line: 1092
    type: narration
    text: "Because freedom was worth any price."
  - line: 1094
    type: narration
    text: "end of chapter 028-ragnarok"

